# Section variety and five-point layouts

## 1 · Adjacent sections cannot share a structure

Two neighboring sections must present content differently. Same background color change is not enough.

Do **not** stack:

- Card grid → card grid (InfoCard, ServiceCard, Features2, handmade cards)
- Icon/text list → icon/text list
- Timeline → timeline
- Comparison table → comparison table
- Full-width narrative (P-13) → full-width narrative

Separate two card sections with a split (P-03), timeline (P-08), table, FAQ, or P-13. Reorder the brief if needed.

A card grid is any boxed item grid. An icon+title+description **list** (no card chrome) is a different structure from cards. A **centered one-row band** (`IconPointBand`) is a different structure from a **2 × 2 text grid** (`IconPointGrid`).

## 2 · Never use a 5-card grid

Do **not** lay out 5 items as cards — not 3+2, not 5-across, not 2+3.

For 5 parallel points use **P-06**: `IconPointBand` — one horizontal row of icon-on-top points (no cards, no timeline rail).

For 5 items that each link to a page, use a **stacked directory** (full-width rows with title, description, link). Not cards.

| Count | Cards OK? | Layout |
|---|---|---|
| 2, 3, 4, 6 | Yes, if the previous section is not also cards | Even grid |
| 5 | No | P-06 icon points, or linked directory rows |
| 7+ | No single card grid | Split the section or use P-08 / P-13 |
